# Red News Project Rules

## Architecture
- Chrome Extension: Manifest V3 (MV3)
- Website: Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS on Cloudflare
- Backend: Supabase (database + auth)
- Payment: Paddle (payment processing)

## Tech Stack
- Language: JavaScript → TypeScript (migration in progress)
- Extension: vanilla JS, no frameworks
- Website: HTML/CSS/JS, vanilla
- Build: esbuild, Webpack (for bundling)
- Testing: Jest (new), Node.js (old tests)

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Follow Conventional Commits (feat: feat(feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:, test:)
- ESLint + Prettier formatting
- Comments in English, strings in i18n files

## Project Phases
1. **Week 1-2:** TypeScript migration for extension
   - shared.js → shared.ts
   - background.js → background.ts
   - inject.js → inject.ts
   - content.js → content.ts
   - popup.js → popup.ts

2. **Week 3-4:** Website improvements (incremental)
   - Landing page enhancements
   - User dashboard
   - Real-time Supabase integration

3. **Week 5:** GitHub Actions CI/CD setup

4. **Week 6:** Documentation and polish

## Important Constraints
- NEVER break the live product (rednews.app)
- KEEP Supabase and Paddle integrations working
- Test locally before committing
- Incremental commits (each feature = 1-2 commits)